<title>USA: Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer gets $800 mln loan.</title>
<headline>Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer gets $800 mln loan.</headline>
<dateline>SANTA MONICA, Calif. 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer Inc said Wednesday its $800 million secured bank financing, underwritten and arranged by J.P. Morgan &amp; Co, has been successfully syndicated.</p>
<p>The $800 million financing is comprised of a $450 million five-year revolving credit, a $250 million six-year amortizing term loan, and a $100 million seven and one half-year amortizing term loan.</p>
<p>Proceeds will be used to finance the acquisition of MGM from Consortium de Realisation and to provide for future working capital needs and other general corporate purposes.</p>
</text>
